  "disposition": "approved",
  "findings": [
    "The complete switched Hamiltonian and thermal uncoupled bath preparation uniquely fix both decoherence and conditional displacement phase; absence of extra Hamiltonian terms excludes a compensating counterterm.",
    "The analytic phase has the correct positive sign for U=exp(-i H t). The density-matrix readout contraction and spin charge ordering match the independent Fock trace.",
    "Calibration with one zero coupling weight has s^2 constant across all spin basis states, so its conditional phase vanishes exactly for arbitrary preparation/readout and both models fit identically.",
    "The supplied shared Gaussian phase channel is a positive, trace-preserving approximation using every known parameter; its missing bath response is a physical approximation, not a broken common-noise average.",
    "Independent reference propagates each conditional finite oscillator Hamiltonian and thermally traces it, and factors the four independent bath contributions. This is structurally distinct from the closed form."
  ],
